Kind: ablation
Issue: #964
Takes out: the refusal of a name of 64 bytes before it is copied: update_driver() copies it and writes its terminator one byte past the name's room, then refuses it as too long for a driver's task.  chora_test [17] reads the same refusal; the HAL's line is another.
Run: --testdev --iommu intel --edu --entry 68 600 -smp 4
Expect: hal: "a{64}", given to update the driver of [0-9a-f]{2}:[0-9a-f]{2}\.[0-7]: its name is empty, or not letters, digits and _, or longer than a driver.s task name has room for
Note: the harness's pair "the HAL refusing a name of 64 bytes" fails too.

